    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first creates a dense feature field, then partitions that field into windows without dropping tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into F, the dense feature field. The window operation takes that same field as its input. X is the partitioned token set, so the equation preserves the carrier rather than replacing it.",
